I'll help you fix the failing tests. Let me start by running the tests to see what's failing, then identify and fix the bug in src/parse.py.
Perfect! I found the bug. The issue is an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function is returning `parts[1]` (the second element) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element).

This causes:
1. `test_basic` to fail: `first_word('hello world')` returns 'world' instead of 'hello'
2. `test_single` to error: `first_word('solo')` tries to access index 1 when only index 0 exists
Perfect! All tests are now passing. The bug was a classic off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]`, which meant it was returning the second word instead of the first word. I changed it to correctly return `parts[0]`, and now both tests pass successfully.
